{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "war-economic-impact-api-v2",
    "name": "War Economic Impact API",
    "description": "# War Economic Impact API\n\nA production-grade REST API for researching and managing the macroeconomic consequences of global armed conflicts.\n\n**Live Base URL:** `https://war-economic-impact-dataset-rishikesh.onrender.com`\n\n**Local Base URL:** `http://localhost:5050`\n\n---\n\n## 🔐 Authentication\nThis API uses **JWT Bearer Tokens**. After calling `Register` or `Login`, the token is automatically stored in the `jwt_token` environment variable via the test script. All protected routes read from `{{jwt_token}}`.\n\n## 📋 How to Use\n1. Select the **War Economic Impact - Environment** from the top-right environment dropdown.\n2. Run **Register User** or **Login User** — the token is auto-saved.\n3. All protected requests will automatically inject the token in the `Authorization: Bearer` header.\n4. To test against your live server, set `base_url` to `https://war-economic-impact-dataset-rishikesh.onrender.com`.\n\n## 📦 Response Envelope\nAll responses follow this standardised format:\n```json\n{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"message\": \"Operation description\",\n  \"data\": {},\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"currentPage\": 1,\n    \"totalPages\": 5,\n    \"totalCount\": 42,\n    \"limit\": 10\n  }\n}\n```",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "https://war-economic-impact-dataset-rishikesh.onrender.com",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Base URL for the API. Change to http://localhost:5050 for local development."
    },
    {
      "key": "jwt_token",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "JWT token auto-populated by the Login or Register test scripts."
    },
    {
      "key": "conflict_id",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "MongoDB ObjectId of a conflict record. Copy an _id from any GET /conflicts response."
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "🔐 Auth",
      "description": "Endpoints for user registration, login, profile retrieval, and logout. Tokens are automatically captured from Register and Login responses.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register User",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "// Auto-save token to environment variable",
                  "if (jsonData.success && jsonData.data && jsonData.data.token) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('jwt_token', jsonData.data.token);",
                  "    console.log('✅ JWT token saved:', jsonData.data.token.substring(0, 20) + '...');",
                  "}",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Status code is 201 Created', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Response has success: true', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.success).to.be.true;",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Response contains JWT token', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.data.token).to.be.a('string');",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.data.token.length).to.be.greaterThan(10);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Response time is under 3000ms', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.responseTime).to.be.below(3000);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Rishikesh Singh\",\n  \"email\": \"rishikesh@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"securepassword123\",\n  \"role\": \"admin\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/auth/register",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "register"]
            },
            "description": "Register a new researcher account.\n\n**Access:** Public\n\n**Required fields:**\n- `name` (string) — Full display name\n- `email` (string) — Valid email address (must be unique)\n- `password` (string) — Minimum 6 characters\n\n**Optional fields:**\n- `role` (string) — `user` (default) or `admin`\n\n**Returns:** User profile object + signed JWT token.\n\n> ⚡ The test script automatically saves the `token` to the `jwt_token` collection variable."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Login User",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "// Auto-save token to collection variable",
                  "if (jsonData.success && jsonData.data && jsonData.data.token) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('jwt_token', jsonData.data.token);",
                  "    console.log('✅ JWT token saved:', jsonData.data.token.substring(0, 20) + '...');",
                  "}",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200 OK', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Login successful - success is true', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.success).to.be.true;",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Token is returned in response', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.data.token).to.be.a('string');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Response time is under 3000ms', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.responseTime).to.be.below(3000);",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"rishikesh@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"securepassword123\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Authenticate a registered user with email and password.\n\n**Access:** Public\n\n**Required fields:**\n- `email` (string) — Registered email address\n- `password` (string) — Account password\n\n**Returns:** User profile object + signed JWT token.\n\n> ⚡ The test script automatically saves the `token` to the `jwt_token` collection variable."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get My Profile (Me)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200 OK', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Profile data is returned', function () {",
                  "    const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.data).to.have.property('email');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{jwt_token}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/auth/me",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "me"]
            },
            "description": "Retrieve the profile of the currently authenticated user.\n\n**Access:** 🔒 Private — requires `Authorization: Bearer {{jwt_token}}`\n\n**Returns:** User profile object (name, email, role, createdAt)."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Logout User",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200 OK', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "// Clear the token on logout",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('jwt_token', '');",
                  "console.log('🔒 JWT token cleared.');"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{jwt_token}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/auth/logout",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "logout"]
            },
            "description": "Invalidate the current user session token.\n\n**Access:** 🔒 Private — requires `Authorization: Bearer {{jwt_token}}`\n\n> ⚡ The test script automatically clears the `jwt_token` collection variable after logout."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "📋 Conflicts — CRUD",
      "description": "Create, Read, Update, and Delete conflict records. GET endpoints are public. POST, PUT, PATCH require authentication. DELETE requires admin role.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get All Conflicts (Paginated)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Status code is 200 OK', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Response has success: true', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.success).to.be.true;",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Data is an array', function () {",
